  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\nI=\\int_{-3 \\pi / 2}^{-\\pi / 2}\\left[(x+\\pi)^3+\\cos ^2(x+3 \\pi)\\right] d x\n$$\nPut $\\mathrm{x}+\\pi=\\mathrm{t}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& I=\\int_{-\\pi / 2}^{\\pi / 2}\\left[t^3+\\cos ^2 t\\right] d t=2 \\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\cos ^2 t d t \\\\\n& =\\int_0^{\\pi / 2}(1+\\cos 2 t) d t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+0 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
